Subject: [PATCH 01167/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for ArcMemo
 SOLVE-transfer v4 (self-learning MANDATE; extends the exp4005 14->10 win to
 .371's NEW content): exp4005 showed concept-memory-seeded solving cut actions
 14->10 on new content. This tests whether the SAME concept memory makes THIS
 milestone's new content cheaper: the higher level from exp4014 OR the 5th
 game from exp4015 (or a re-held-out solved level if neither advanced). Two
 arms at equal perception: (A) cold-start (no memory), (B)
 concept-memory-seeded (retrieve+try the banked concepts: 'select-then-place'
 r11l, 'permute-set' lp85, 'pattern-match-then-navigate' sc25,
 'lattice-step-toward-target' su15 + any new concept). Does retrieving banked
 concepts reduce ACTIONS/ATTEMPTS to solve genuinely NEW content vs
 cold-start? Tier-2 constraint memory (research-program.md) compounding across
 the milestone's own progress. POSITIVE CONTROL: the target must share
 structure with >=2 banked concepts (else transfer is impossible by
 construction; FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK).

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
